            "review_title": "Review at Fork Saigon",
            "review_text": "Duane R\nConroe, Texas63 contributions\n0\nA western style surprise in Saigon\nJan 2018 • Couples\nMy wife and I were on a group tour of SE Asia and had the night on our own when we were drawn to this quaint but stylish establishment. The name automatically drew our attention because of our American eating habits. The restaurant only holds a small number of tables but placed in a design that offers an intimate setting. Smooth jazz is piped overhead and a healthy selection of wine is available. The menu consists of sharing plates and offers a unique variety of dishes for a couple or small group to taste. We had the on menu items and some specials of the day—Shrimp Pil Pil, scallops with risotto, baked oysters, beef cheek (so tender!), tuna carpaccio and finished with a generously supplied dessert of a small brownie with whipped cream topped with a sliced strawberry. All of the food was accompanied by a French bottle of white wine and two glasses of a Spanish red wine. The serving staff was attentive and spoke good English. The proprietor was standing at the bar and added to our very satisfied evening in faraway Ho Chi Minh City. This restaurant would compete extremely well in our hometown of Houston, Texas. For tourists seeking a break from rice, Fork is an outstanding choice.\nRead more\nWritten January 25, 2018",
