            "review_title": "Review at Fork Saigon",
            "review_text": "Lapidus\nAustralia64 contributions\n0\nStunning Food in an Informal Setting\nJan 2018 • Couples\nThis is a companion restaurant to Ciao Bella and Saffron, all in the same area, and all known for their superb food. This was the third or fourth time we have visited and each time we have been impressed by the high standard of food and service.\n\nUnlike the other two restaurants, this restaurant is share plates with a menu that includes tapas, croquettes, fish, meats and vegetables as well as deserts. The plates are incredibly well chosen; our all time favourite is the marmite and mayonaisse baked oysters. Stunning! The tuna carpaccio and the braised beef cheek in a creamed cauliflower sauce are also favourites. \n\nGood wine list too\n\nIt is great to see such a high standard of food delivered with no fuss and at a reasonable price. You are dining in a potential michelin starred restaurant.\n\nHighly recommended\nRead more\nService\nFood\nWritten January 17, 2018",
